  "id": "licking-behavior",
  "term": "licking behavior",
  "definition": "Licking behavior is the rhythmic tongue activity animals use to consume palatable liquids such as sucrose. In this source, it is treated as a measurable part of consummatory behavior that can be disrupted or altered by changes in nucleus accumbens D2 neuron activity and its timing.",
